// The talent trees (key N): three trees of perks, drawn in the original's talent window (7 tiers, 4 columns; a tier opens with 5 points
// spent in its tree per tier before it). One point per level from level 10.
//
// Per talent: `tier` 1-7 and `column` 1-4 (its place), `ranks` (how many points it takes), `perk` (what ONE rank gives, see `talents::Perk`;
// percent or percentage points), `text` (the tooltip: `{}` is the total of the ranks learned), `requires` (the id of a talent of the same tree that
// must have all its ranks first), `needs` (tree number 0-2 and points: a hybrid talent asks for points spent in another tree).
// Trees: 0 Warfare (strength), 1 Sorcery (mana), 2 Skirmisher (agility). Attributes: 0 strength, 1 agility, 2 stamina, 3 intellect, 4 spirit.
// Spell perks work on every spell the character knows: SpellPower (all), ClassPower (the spells of one class, as the spellbook's tabs group them), SpellCost,
// Cooldown and CastTime (percent less).
